<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; Codex Tibetan-first PROVISIONAL machine alignment; not human-approved. The opponent grants human perception validity but attributes the other two perceptions to karma. The same two visual-consciousness and valid-perception occurrences are individually pinned. las owns karma, supported in the preserved original glossary although the curated unified equivalent is deeds. dbang owns forces; objects/participants in forces them to stay unwrapped. sogs owns like, not the supplied something. de la owns the complete case frame In the case mentioned at phrase depth; kho na re owns Someone may answer at phrase depth, both positive original HGM glossary recasts. The later de owns These; latter and types of remain supplied. The closing zer na and expanded with the following claim are distributed reporting, omitted rather than falsely nulled. Unaligned case particles and the second yin pa are omitted; no separate-exponent judgment is claimed. All source wording remains unchanged.</div>
